 "be_addendum_notes": {
  "ADDED_POST_GENERATION": true,
  "BEATING_RANDOM_IS_NOT_BEATING_THE_INCUMBENT": "All four arms passed the receipt's random-canceller gate. On the arm-vs-arm question the gate never asked, 10 of 12 cells are indistinguishable from chance after joint correction.",
  "G_AND_THE_CONSUMED_DAY": "G = 0 complete UTC days on BOTH coins. The entire scoring population is a single 14.4-hour span on 2026-08-25 (slug floor 1787650200 = 2026-08-25T09:30:00Z). 08-25 is inside the consumed range 08-20..25 named in CLAUDE.md rule 11. So the day-cluster unit has zero replicates, no interval is claimable, and this population cannot serve as the validation rule 11 requires: later untouched days, >= 5 complete UTC days.",
  "NON_MONOTONE_IN_BUDGET": "Both btc arms COLLAPSE at 15%: LGBM_PINNED raw p 0.6677, PLUS_PRED_STATE_V1 raw p 0.2144, against 0.0015-0.0305 at 5/10%. An increment that appears at two budgets and vanishes at the third is not a stable effect; no mechanism has been offered for why 15% should erase it.",
  "POPULATION_IS_DEVELOPMENT_NOT_TEST": "phase2_declaration.POPULATION == 'da_development_topup'. The scoring surface is the DEVELOPMENT top-up. This is a discriminator among candidates, NOT a validation of one.",
  "P_VALUES_ARE_OPTIMISTIC": "The permutation unit is the WINDOW because the ruled unit (UTC day) has no replicates here. Windows within a day are not independent, so every p above is an under-estimate of the true value. The two surviving cells survive against an optimistic null.",
  "WHAT_SURVIVES_JOINT_CORRECTION": "Two cells of twelve: btc/LGBM_PINNED@10% (Holm 0.0180) and btc/LGBM_PINNED@5% (Holm 0.0220). PLUS_PRED_STATE_V1 survives NOWHERE \u2014 its best cell is btc@10% at Holm 0.0700. On eth NOTHING survives on either arm, and LGBM_PINNED's eth increments are NEGATIVE at all three budgets.",
  "WHAT_THIS_DOES_AND_DOES_NOT_SUPPORT": "SUPPORTS: btc LGBM_PINNED's increment over the incumbent at 5/10% is unlikely to be pure window-level noise on this development day. DOES NOT SUPPORT: any freeze as a validated result; any eth claim on either arm; any PLUS_PRED_STATE_V1 claim once the 12 cells are read jointly, which is how they were declared to be read.",
  "added_by": "BE at commit time; the CELLS and p-values above are the run's own output, unmodified",
  "analysis_code_ref": "2152a3a4913b5ee6a66b05496fa95ce3a37e52c2",
  "analysis_code_ref_why_recorded_here": "provenance.fit_code_ref names the FIT that produced the scored artifacts (19b0611). It does NOT name the analysis code that produced these numbers. Both refs are legitimate and different. Recorded because fit_code_ref is env-supplied \u2014 the manifest verifies a label was passed, not that code ran \u2014 and binding code by MEASUREMENT is an open debt."
 },
